== 7. Verdict against the pre-set criterion ==================== 
  RASSF9 vs total burden: ABSENT 
    rho = -0.008, BH p = 0.864 | adjusted beta -0.0586 (p = 0.321) 
  RASSF10 vs total burden: ASSOCIATION PRESENT 
    rho = -0.161, BH p = 0.002 | adjusted beta -0.2554 (p = 1.60e-04), 78% retained 
 
  WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY, and it should be stated in any write-up: 
  these are cross-sectional bulk measurements of resected tumours. 
  An association, if present, does not establish that burden causes 
  repression of RASSF9, that repression drives progression, or the 
  direction of any arrow. A tumour that is more mutated and has less 
  RASSF9 is consistent with repression, with selection, with 
  differing cell composition, and with reverse causation equally. 
 
  FURTHER: RASSF9 in bulk tumour is largely non-melanocytic across 
  three platforms, so any burden association measured in bulk may 
  reflect stromal and vascular content rather than melanocyte 
  biology, whatever the purity adjustment shows. 

